Playing in the tournament I've just managed to sneak myself an ascension
in before it ends on Thursday.  I'm no expert so I've been playing
Valks, and figured I'd try lawful for a change, so spent most of the
game wielding Excalibur and throwing +7 daggers.  Swapped it for Fire
Brand eventually when that showed up in Vlad's tower.

Didn't make many notes, but there was an altar on dlvl 4, sokoban had
reflection, and I found an early wand of wishing in the mines, which
helped tremendously.  Oh, and I'd done the unknown challenge already on
an earlier game, which made life easier.  I left it last night just
before heading up Rodney's tower to wake him up, with everything pretty
much in place.  So this morning I hacked my way up and then foolishly
attacked him while standing on the ice I'd made of his moat, and fell in
blanking my cursed scrolls of teleport.

He double troubled me in the tower, and again in the sanctum, but it
wasn't too tough.  A cockatrice conveniently died just outside, and I
very carefully didn't move while wielding it, after my last decent game
in the tournament where I feel in the same pit wielding the same corpse
twice in a row.  D'oh.

Got back up to my stash on dlvl 1, dropped a bunch of stuff which I was
a bit burdened by while I did some alchemy for spare full healing
potions, picked up my stuff, checked I had the real amulet by trying to
bag it and went up the stairs wielding a blessed potion of paralysis
which I promptly hit rodney over the head with.  It was taking a while
to kill him though, so I thought I'd try to finish it quickly with the
wand of death.  Wand of death, hmm, I'm sure I had one a minute ago.
Look in bag.  Fuck.  I didn't pick up the stack of wands.  Here I am in
the planes with no wands at all.

Amazingly I survived.  I'd got my gold detection scrolls and ring of
levitation, was pretty buff, and had food as well as healing and holy
water, so I just battled through.  Rodney dropped one wand of digging
too, so that got me through Earth.  Fire was a doddle.  Air was much
tougher though, I wasn't having much trouble getting across to the
portal then Rodney appeared, summoned a million pets and his double, and
was a complete nuisance.  I found myself wondering what would happen if
an air E moved onto the portal while I was inside and Rodney had the
amulet.  It didn't come to that though, and he eventually died and
handed it over - I killed him 8 times in all.  Water was a walkover,
since I'd genocided L, h, and ; long ago.

Spotted pesty at far left altar so figured I'd leave that til last.
Picked up a wand of death over near the far right though which did for
famine once, letting me get to that altar and discover it was in fact
Odin's.  Battled back (killing famine again by hitting him lots, and
scoffing k-rations), and killed death quickly, scooted round the
remaining monsters to the middle altar, and it was mine!  Offer the
amulet to Tyr:

An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...--More--

Hurray!  Left me all weak and wobbly with excitement, but I've done it!

Only my second ever, and the first in the tournament.

